# Lunaris Dolby

A privileged Android app for controlling Dolby audio features exposed by the device's audio stack.

## This repository

This fork contains the app only. It does not ship the Dolby DMS HAL, Codec2 decoders, proprietary vendor libraries, VINTF declarations, init services, or vendor SELinux policy. The app alone does not provide Dolby audio processing or codec support.

## Build and package

Build the app with the Android build system:

```sh
m LunarisDolby
```

Add `LunarisDolby` to the product package list:

```makefile
PRODUCT_PACKAGES += LunarisDolby
```

The build target includes the app's preinstalled-package and privileged-permission declarations.

## Device audio integration

The device or a separate hardware Dolby project must provide a compatible Dolby backend. Integrate the backend components in the device/vendor tree, including the required audio effects registration, media codec configuration, VINTF declarations, init services, and SELinux policy.

The full Dolby integration can support AC-3, E-AC-3, E-AC-3 JOC, and AC-4 decoding, along with software or hardware Dolby Audio Processing (DAP), depending on the device and its vendor libraries. Select and configure only the backend supported by the device. Those codecs, libraries, and integration files are outside this app-only repository.
